thmic improvement.\n379:Large language models were used extensively and are disclosed here. An autonomous LLM-based research agent proposed the study design within the task's constraints. The evaluated perturbation finder was not written by the agent: it is the provided starter (baseline) configuration, seeded before the search. The agent designed three refined search configurations, but their source is not among our artifacts and none was scored. The agent wrote the analysis and plotting scripts and drafted this manuscript, including its framing and text. Every number in the paper comes from the sealed evaluation record produced by executing the code, and the derivation scripts are included. Bibliographic metadata was retrieved from the Semantic Scholar API. Huang et al.~(2025) is cited by title only, as part of the provided background reading list. No result or method in this paper is taken from it. No paid API or GPU was used for the experiments.\n143:      \"claim\": \"The sealed evaluation completed, qualified, and passed all validity gates.\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
